padconnect — locally modified scrcpy-android distribution

This repository preserves upstream source notices and license files.
Local modifications and integration are maintained by ssuper1, 2026.
This is an independent modified version, not an official upstream release.

scrcpy-android
  Source: https://gitlab.com/0xlena/scrcpy-android
  Base commit: 4341eb16f2ff3233599b1f42c91105f424bc016a (0.5)
  License: Apache License 2.0; see scrcpy-android/LICENSE.
  Local changes include Android compatibility repairs, a phone-shaped virtual
  display, remote application selection, display density controls, rotation,
  immersive controller UI, an edge menu, Chinese resources, and associated tests.
  Build configuration, embedded server assets and root integration also differ
  from upstream. See PHONE-MODE.md and Git history for details.

scrcpy
  Source: https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy
  Base commit: 2926c06c5dc3064ae6d8db706f1a98a37cfcf3f0 (4.1)
  License: Apache License 2.0; see scrcpy-android/vendor/scrcpy/LICENSE.
  Local changes: server/build.gradle and
  server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/video/NewDisplayCapture.java;
  added server/src/test/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/video/NewDisplayCaptureTest.java.
  Virtual display rendering dimensions are separated from encoded video size.
  The embedded server binary is built from this modified source.

libadb-android
  Source: https://github.com/MuntashirAkon/libadb-android
  Vendored base recorded by scrcpy-android: 3.1.1,
  c849886ebc6d48e7b46d967e78a6bb65c90c3b74.
  Vendored integration includes the changes described in its README.
  See scrcpy-android/vendor/libadb-android/COPYING and LICENSES/ for its
  license choices, bundled component licenses and copyright notices.

The upstream repositories are vendored as ordinary files here, including
local changes. Upstream license and copyright notices remain in place.
